From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Updates menu: add "UPDATE TO AANZE NIGHTLY" entry

Add a second software-update action directly under the stock START UPDATE
entry in the "UPDATES & DOWNLOADS" > "SOFTWARE UPDATES" menu, targeting the
personal nightly releases published at github.com/aanze/distribution instead
of the official update.rocknix.org endpoint.

Rather than duplicate the whole download/verify/progress/reboot UX, the patch
parameterises the single hardcoded "rocknix-update" command string through the
existing flow:

  - ApiSystem::updateSystem() and ApiSystem::canUpdate() gain an optional
    `updatecommand` argument (default "rocknix-update"), so behaviour for all
    existing callers is unchanged.
  - GuiUpdate (and its inner ThreadedUpdater) gain an optional `updateCommand`
    that is threaded through to canUpdate()/updateSystem().
  - GuiMenu pushes `new GuiUpdate(mWindow, "aanze-update")` for the new entry.

The aanze-update backend script mirrors rocknix-update's contract (`check`
prints the available version and exits 0 when an update is available; the
default mode stages the verified tarball into /storage/.update and returns 0),
so staging + apply-on-reboot via the busybox init updater are identical to the
official path.

---
diff --git a/es-app/src/ApiSystem.cpp b/es-app/src/ApiSystem.cpp
index a5b8e9be..72cca7a6 100644
--- a/es-app/src/ApiSystem.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/ApiSystem.cpp
@@ -188,11 +188,10 @@ bool ApiSystem::setOverclock(std::string mode)
 }
 
 // BusyComponent* ui
-std::pair<std::string, int> ApiSystem::updateSystem(const std::function<void(const std::string)>& func)
+std::pair<std::string, int> ApiSystem::updateSystem(const std::function<void(const std::string)>& func, const std::string& updatecommand)
 {
 	LOG(LogDebug) << "ApiSystem::updateSystem";
 
-	std::string updatecommand = "rocknix-update";
 
 	FILE *pipe = popen(updatecommand.c_str(), "r");
 	if (pipe == nullptr)
@@ -325,11 +324,11 @@ bool ApiSystem::ping()
     return true;
 }
 
-bool ApiSystem::canUpdate(std::vector<std::string>& output) 
+bool ApiSystem::canUpdate(std::vector<std::string>& output, const std::string& updatecommand)
 {
 	LOG(LogDebug) << "ApiSystem::canUpdate";
 
-	FILE *pipe = popen("rocknix-update check", "r");
+	FILE *pipe = popen((updatecommand + " check").c_str(), "r");
 	if (pipe == NULL)
 		return false;
 
